{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_09-22-17-omnipaxos-real-run/draft && timeout 200 python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nCH=\\\"27a729f8adb440c2b845ef833c3a16ec-question-0\\\"; R=\\\"e70b8baa087246c78ea3a64f24b8e97c\\\"\ninterp={\\\"investigation_id\\\":CH,\\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"a9cad483efbe4868a0d1c52a13253499-experiment\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"snapshot_decided_bound_doc\\\",\\\"try_snapshot_decided_bound\\\",\\\"create_snapshot_range\\\",\\\"internal_read_range\\\",\\\"memory_storage_read_helpers\\\",\\\"create_log_sync\\\",\\\"sync_log_accounting\\\",\\\"no_stopsign_decided_idx\\\"],\n \\\"executions\\\":{R:[0,1,2,3,4,5]},\n \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"violated\\\",\\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n \\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"Witnessed, and the variants named in this question's discriminator are now narrowed by source with one earlier counter-argument corrected. Witness: with the drift in place (accepted 9, 9 and 6, decided 9, content six indices), snapshot(Some(8), false) returned Ok, the leader's compacted index became 8, and the snapshot reachable at index 0 held zero entry ids where the log had five decided entries (e70b8baa087246c78ea3a64f24b8e97c events 0-5); the comparisons requiring the compacted index to reach six and the snapshot to hold five entries were violated at the call event. Correction of an earlier counter-argument: I had written that the StopSign adjustment of the equal case might keep ordinary requests inside the entries; measured against the observed state it does not - a request equal to the drifted decided index would be mapped to the decided log without the StopSign, which is 8 rather than 9, and 8 still exceeds the content 6, so the equal case is not a protection here. Follower-side variant: the bound is computed from the decided index of the node that receives the call, so a follower whose own decided index has drifted the same way would accept the same request, with local_only only deciding whether the compaction is forwarded to the peers. Entry-type dependence: the loss takes the form the entry type's Snapshot::create gives to an empty slice; here that is an empty snapshot, and the reads then report a snapshotted region whose payload holds nothing.\\\"),\n \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\\\"The call itself returned Ok, so nothing in its result signals the loss; the witness is the compacted index together with the number of entries the produced snapshot holds.\\\",\n  \\\"The user supplied the index 8; the documented note allows any index up to the decided index, which was 9, so the request was inside the documented allowance rather than a caller error.\\\",\n  \\\"The apparent protection offered by the equal case does not hold in the observed state: it lowers the bound from 9 to 8, which is still above the content (6).\\\"],\n \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"The consequence depends on the entry type's snapshot: here the snapshot records its input entries and is empty for an empty slice; an entry type that reconstructs state differently could behave differently.\\\",\n  \\\"The snapshot was requested with local_only false, so peers receive the forwarded compaction; their own compactions were sampled only through their accepted and decided indexes (events 4 and 5), not through their snapshots.\\\",\n  \\\"One three-node configuration, three reconnection rounds, one index and one entry type were exercised; the follower-side variant and the equal-index variant are argued from the derivation, not executed.\\\",\n  \\\"The comparisons that would tie the before and after samples to their admissions are unknown because of a shared event name in the same execution; the states are asserted from the sampled operands (events 0-5).\\\"],\n \\\"joint_history\\\":(\\\"Same harness lineage as the drift account: receipt e70b8baa087246c78ea3a64f24b8e97c ran experiment a9cad483efbe4868a0d1c52a13253499-experiment, whose snap case reproduces receipt fd0b8be59c8f466fbf7768abb08f93b5 and whose new case uses the same snapshot-capable entry type and the same three reconnection rounds as the trim receipt ec3329dc273e452aa92bcd44652c116a; each case is read on its own samples and no measurement is combined across executions.\\\"),\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[{\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"27a729f8adb440c2b845ef833c3a16ec-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"the snapshot bound comes from the decided index alone\\\"},\n  {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"856d6fe2b3a14c7ab6dbed00026ba199-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"the snapshot path accepted a drifted bound and produced a snapshot holding none of the entries\\\"},\n  {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"e65d63f4057d4c5bbe8390ac06b30fce-knowledge-2\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"the recorded accepted and decided indexes drift one index per re-synchronization round\\\"}]}\nup={\\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"Narrow two of the snapshot question's remaining variants by source and correct one earlier counter-argument, without another execution. The correction: the StopSign adjustment of the equal case does not protect in the observed state, because it maps a request equal to the drifted decided index to the decided log without the StopSign (8) which is still above the content (6). The narrowings: the bound is computed on the node that receives the call, so a follower with the same drifted decided index would accept the same request, and local_only only controls forwarding; the form of the loss is whatever the entry type's Snapshot::create does with an empty slice. The account keeps its violated/asserted judgment on the same receipt.\\\"),\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[interp]}\njson.dump(up, open('update.json','w'), indent=1); print('written')\nPY\ntimeout 120 /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_09-22-17-omnipaxos-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -c 600\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
